  await mongo.collection('workouts').insertOne({ userId, sessionId: session.id, startedAt: session.startedAt });
  await redis.set(`user:${userId}:last_session`, session.id, 'EX', 3600);
  await cassandra.execute("UPDATE hourly_agg SET ...", [userId, session]);
  await dynamo.updateItem({ /* weekly summary increment */ });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test TTL expiry and cross-store invalidation?
- How would you handle partial failures and ensure idempotent retries?

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes whether the candidate can reason about ACID guarantees in a distributed, MVCC environment and reason about cross-shard coordination and realistic failure modes.

## Key Concepts
- SERIALIZABLE semantics and MVCC
- Phantom reads and write skew
- SELECT FOR UPDATE and distributed locking
- Cross-shard coordination, idempotent retries, cache invalidation

